+## Context
+
+Fresh TypeScript repo, no runtime dependencies, tests via `node --test`, nothing under `src/` yet.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** in-memory rental service obeying the school's five rules.
+**Non-Goals:** cancellations/refunds, persistence, availability search.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Files: everything lives in `src/index.ts` (no relative imports, so it runs under Node type stripping); tests in `src/index.test.ts`. Each service instance owns its own state.
+- Time: parse with a strict regex for `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS(.fff)?Z`, check the date is real, require midnight; days = (end − start) / 86 400 000 (UTC has no DST). `start`/`end` are echoed back as given.
+- Money: `total = dailyPrice × days`, integers only; `dailyPrice` validated as a non-negative safe integer.
+- Overlap: half-open intervals `[start, end)`; conflict iff `start < otherEnd && otherStart < end`, per item.
+- Booking ids: sequential counter-based string (e.g. `bk-1`), unique per service.
+- Cancellation: not implemented; the 24 h / full-refund policy is kept in the spec for the later change. Bookings keep `start` and `total`, which that policy needs.
+- Tests: `.test.ts` run directly by `node --test` via Node type stripping.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Assumption: zero price is allowed; duplicate item ids are rejected.
+- Non-`Z` offsets (even `+00:00`) are rejected for simplicity.
